{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION to the stopgap I recorded above (operator-revised): TRIVIAL must be overridden too - export REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 AND export REBAR_LLM_TRIVIAL_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8. The original 'leave TRIVIAL alone' was justified on schema size - sound for grammar compilation, but irrelevant to the variant that bites on this host, where EVERY native structured-output call fails regardless of schema size. Stopgap validated end-to-end on a real gate run: unmitigated -> 1 grammar 400, INDETERMINATE, verify_failed true, blocking 0 / indeterminate 6; with stopgap -> 0 grammar 400s, verdict BLOCK with real findings (unsigned both times but for opposite reasons - the second is the gate WORKING)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785959401314034001,"uuid":"961dcee5-850a-4965-a524-540c7af4638a"}